'''Jonathan Lowell Spencer "Johnny" Storm''' was a member of the [[Fantastic Four/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Fantastic Four]] known as '''Human Torch'''. He was pruned by the [[Time Variance Authority]] and sent to the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], where he joined the [[Resistance]] opposing [[Cassandra Nova]] and her [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|henchmen]]. Human Torch was captured along with [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] by a group of Nova's scavengers led by [[Pyro]], who stripped Storm of his powers. When Deadpool openly mentioned Storm's vulgar comments about her, Nova brutally killed him.

==Biography==
{{MD|Jonathan Storm (Earth-121698)||1}}
===Early Life===
====The Fantastic Four====
Following a mission in space, Johnny Storm gained the power to manipulate and transform his body into fire, which granted him the ability to fly. Along with three others who also possessed unique powers, including [[Mister Fantastic/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Reed Richards]], they formed a superhero team known as the [[Fantastic Four/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Fantastic Four]], with Storm going by the codename "Human Torch."{{Ref|DW}}

===Banished to the Void===
====Encounter with the TVA====
{{Quote|You're in the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]]. Think of it as purgatory. [[Mister Fantastic/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Reed]] called it a metaphysical junkyard where anything useless goes before it gets annihilated forever. And where the [[TVA]] sends people that don't play nice with the rest of the [[Multiverse]]."<br>"Like you?|Human Torch and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
At some point, Human Torch had a run in with the [[Multiverse]] which resulted in him being taken by the [[Time Variance Authority]], who pruned him, sending him to the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], a place that [[Mister Fantastic/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Mister Fantastic]] had researched and expressed thoughts on. Human Torch was able to avoid being eaten by [[Alioth]], but others he was with were not so fortunate.{{Ref|DW}}

====Joining the Resistance====
{{Quote|Everyone here's on the run from [[Alioth]]. Most don't make it. There's a [[Resistance]] though. Other people like us that managed to survive. They're hiding out in the borderlands trying to find a way the fuck out of here.|Human Torch to [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Human Torch came across a group of other heroes who had survived in the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]] from [[Alioth]]. However, the wasteland was ruled by the [[mutant]] [[Cassandra Nova]], who forced those trapped in the Void to work for her. This group of heroes, including [[Elektra/Forgotten Elektra|Elektra]], [[Blade/Universe Defender Blade|Blade]], [[Gambit]], and [[X-23]], rebelled against Nova and formed a [[Resistance]], hiding out in the borderlands and trying to figure a way out of the Void. The Resistance spent years in hiding, and any attempt they made to fight Nova only ended in defeat.{{Ref|DW}}

====Meeting Deadpool and Wolverine====
[[File:Johnny Storm meets Deadpool & Wolverine.png|{{AltFloat}}|Human Torch calls [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]]]
{{Quote|In fact, I don't give a shit if [[Cassandra Nova|she]] removes all my skin and pops me like some nightmarish blood balloon. If the last thing I do in this godforsaken, cum-gutter existence is light that fuck-box on fire, I still won't die happy!|Johnny Storm and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Human Torch went out on a scout mission, during which he came across [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]], who were in the middle of [[Duel in the Void|fighting]] each other. Human Torch broke it up by telling them that fighting each other meant that they would lose and warned them that [[Cassandra Nova]]'s [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|crew]] were approaching their location. Jumping to the ground, Human Torch revealed himself, which excited Deadpool.
[[File:Johnny Storm, Deadpool and Wolverine.png|{{AltFloat}}|Human Torch prepares to fight against [[Pyro]]]]
As they became surrounded by a convoy of Nova's henchmen led by [[Pyro]], Human Torch confidently told Deadpool and Wolverine that he would handle the situation. Deadpool hugged Human Torch from the back, who broke free from him as Pyro told them there was nowhere to run. Human Torch responded that he wasn't running and warned Pyro of what was about to come. Human Torch then shouted his catchphrase and ignited into flames.
[[File:Human Torch is depowered.png|{{AltFloat}}|Human Torch's fire is extinguished by [[Pyro]]]]
Soaring into the sky above everyone, Human Torch blasted a beam of fire directly at Pyro. However, also having fire-based powers, Pyro was able to stop Human Torch's attack with ease and extinguish all of his fire. Rendered powerless, Human Torch plummeted from the sky, hitting a nearby structure on the way down before crashing onto the ground, knocking him unconscious. Human Torch was tied up and thrown in a cage alongside Deadpool and Wolverine, who were also defeated by the henchmen.
[[File:Johnny Storm discusses the Void.png|{{AltFloat}}|Human Torch talks about [[Cassandra Nova]]]]
As they were taken to Nova's [[Cassandra Nova's Lair|lair]], Human Torch explained the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], using [[Mister Fantastic/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Mister Fantastic]]'s explanation to do so. He informed them about [[Alioth]] and the [[Resistance]]; Wolverine thought the Resistance could help them get back to the [[TVA]], but Human Torch laughed at the idea, stating that whoever didn't get eaten by Alioth worked for Nova. Human Torch then spent the remainder of the trip expressing his hatred for Nova in extremely vulgar language, which he said he could be quoted on.{{Ref|DW}}

====Death====
[[File:Johnny Storm and Cassandra Nova.png|{{AltFloat}}|Human Torch is brought to [[Cassandra Nova]]]]
{{Quote|I have never said any of those words in my entire life."<br>"Ha! The modesty. People think I'm a shit-talker, but this guy... next level.|Human Torch and [[Deadpool]] to [[Cassandra Nova]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Arriving at the [[Cassandra Nova's Lair|compound]], Human Torch, [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] were let out of the cage and brought before [[Cassandra Nova]], who remarked on how she had spent years trying to capture Human Torch.
[[File:Johnny Storm death.png|{{AltFloat}}|Human Torch is killed by [[Cassandra Nova]]]]
Deadpool interrupted, revealing to Nova what Human Torch had told them about her, although Human Torch tried to get Deadpool to stop talking at the risk of getting him killed. However, Deadpool continued and repeated exactly what Human Torch said to them verbatim. Human Torch attempted to deny it all, but Deadpool insisted on crediting Human Torch for his words. In a panic, Human Torch still desperately tried to deny insulting Nova, but she coldly used her powers to remove his skin in an instant. In his final seconds of life, Human Torch managed to blink in shock before his whole body fell apart.{{Ref|DW}}

===Legacy===
{{Quote|I'm tired of these absolutely vile rumors that I got Johnny killed. Let's take a look at the tape.|[[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
[[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] were able to [[Escape from Cassandra Nova's Lair|escape]] from [[Cassandra Nova]]'s [[Cassandra Nova's Lair|compound]] when [[Alioth]] arrived, and they later were brought to the [[Hero Hideout]] by the [[Resistance]]. Deadpool rallied the group to launch an [[Assault on Cassandra Nova's Lair|attack]] on Nova's compound in the hopes of using Nova to finally escape the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], citing Human Torch's death as a reason. The Resistance was saddened to hear that Human Torch had been murdered, but Wolverine accused Deadpool of getting him killed, which the latter denied.

The attack was successful, allowing Deadpool and Wolverine to return to the former's [[Earth-10005|universe]] in time to stop Nova from using the [[Time Ripper]] to destroy all universes but the Void. Returning to the [[Time Variance Authority]] [[Time Variance Authority Office|Office]], Deadpool retrieved and played a tape taken from a hidden camera that was located in his cage. The tape showed Human Torch insulting and demeaning Nova using incredibly crude language, proving that he said the things Deadpool accused him of.{{Ref|DW}}

==Powers and Abilities==
===Powers===
*'''Fire Manipulation''': [[File:Johnny Storm Human Torch (Void).png|thumb|250px|Human Torch sets himself on fire]] Human Torch had the power to manipulate fire, which formed around his body when he used his abilities. He could channel this fire in the form of blasts and beams.
**'''Flight''': Human Torch could use this force to fly, which he did when battling [[Pyro]]. However, Pyro's own ability to manipulate fire negated Human Torch's abilities.
*'''Superhuman Durability''': Storm's superhuman nature granted him the ability to greatly withstand attacks and falls, as he fell from the sky in the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], landed on his groin on a railing, and proceeded to hit the ground headfirst, but with no visible injuries.

==Equipment==
*'''[[Fantastic Four Uniform]]''': Storm wore a version of the [[Fantastic Four/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Fantastic Four]] uniform in the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], which is heat-resistant and does not melt even under high temperatures when Storm transforms into Human Torch.

