==Trivia==
*In the {{WPS|Fantastic Four in film#Tim Story films (2005–2007)|''Fantastic Four'' duology}}, Johnny Storm is the impetuous brother of [[Sue Storm]] who joined her, [[Mister Fantastic/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Reed Richards]] and [[Ben Grimm]] on a mission to space. However, they were hit by cosmic radiation, giving them all powers including Johnny's fire manipulation. Human Torch and the [[Fantastic Four/Void-Analyzing Fantastic Four|Fantastic Four]] soon fought an old friend, [[Victor von Doom]] and defeated him. Later on, the Fantastic Four also fought [[Silver Surfer]], who made contact with Johnny, allowing Johnny to take the powers of others on contact. With the combined powers of the Fantastic Four, Johnny was able to defeat Doom again, who had taken Silver Surfer's [[Silver Surfer's Surfboard|surfboard]].

==Behind the Scenes==
*Human Torch in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] continues the live-action incarnation of the character from {{WPS|Tim Story}}'s {{WPS|Fantastic Four in film#Tim Story films (2005–2007)|''Fantastic Four'' duology}} from {{WPS|20th Century Fox}}, who was also portrayed by [[Chris Evans]]; he is the second live-action incarnation of the character, following an incarnation portrayed by [[Jay Underwood]].
**Evans agreed to reprise his role following a text from [[Ryan Reynolds (actor)|Ryan Reynolds]] asking if he'd be willing to. Evans later told ''Entertainment Weekly'' that Reynolds may be the only person he would be willing to reprise the role of Human Torch for.<ref>[https://ew.com/chris-evans-deadpool-and-wolverine-johnny-storm-interview-exclusive-8684326 Chris Evans opens up about ''Deadpool & Wolverine'' role and wearing that suit again (exclusive)]</ref>
*The ''Fantastic Four'' duology's Human Torch appearing in a [[Deadpool]] film with Chris Evans reprising the role was previously considered for ''{{WPS|Deadpool 2}}'', as writer [[Paul Wernick]] revealed that they considered have Evans' Human Torch audition for the {{WPS|X-Force}} interviews, but that discussions on the idea did not go as far as to contact Evans.<ref>[https://uproxx.com/movies/deadpool-2-writers-cut-scenes-rhett-reese-paul-wernick/ The ‘Deadpool 2’ Writers Tell Us About Cut Scenes Featuring Chris Evans And Baby Hitler]</ref>
*The [[List of Post-credits Scenes|post-credits scene]] in which Storm speaks in a vulgar manner about [[Cassandra Nova]] was, according to co-writer [[Ryan Reynolds (actor)|Ryan Reynolds]], written primarily to get [[Chris Evans]] to agree to appear in ''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]''. However, Reynolds was proud of how funny the scene turned out to be and Evans only agreed to do the film if the scene stayed in the final cut.{{Ref|TMoDW}}

